Usage: semaphore-cli evaluate [flags]

⚙️ Evaluate feature flags based on configuration and context

⚙️ Evaluate feature flags based on configuration and context, if no specific
flag requested it will evaluate all flags

Examples:

# Evaluate a specific flag using deprecated flag --config evaluate --config
./config.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using new flag --path evaluate --kind file --path
./config.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using http retriever evaluate --kind http --url
http://localhost:8080/config.yaml --header 'ContentType: application/json'
--header 'X-Auth=Token' --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using github retriever evaluate --kind github
--repository-slug thomaspoignant/go-feature-flag --branch master --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using gitlab retriever evaluate --kind gitlab
--base-url https://gitlab.com --repository-slug thomaspoignant/go-feature-flag
--branch master --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using bitbucket retriever evaluate --kind bitbucket
--repository-slug thomaspoignant/go-feature-flag --branch master --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using s3 retriever evaluate --kind s3 --bucket
my-bucket --item my-item.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using gcs retriever evaluate --kind googleStorage
--bucket my-bucket --object my-item.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey":
"user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using configmap retriever evaluate --kind configmap
--namespace default --config-map my-configmap --key my-key.yaml --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using mongodb retriever evaluate --kind mongodb --uri
mongodb://localhost:27017 --database my-database --collection my-collection
--flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using azureblob retriever evaluate --kind azureblob
--container my-container --account-name my-account-name --account-key
my-account-key --object my-object --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey":
"user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using postgres retriever evaluate --kind postgres
--table my-table --column my-column:my-column-type --flag flag1 --ctx
'{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

Flags:
  -h, --help                      Show context-sensitive help.
  -v, --version                   Print the version and exit

      --header=HEADER             HTTP header to access your configuration file
                                  on HTTP (may be repeated)
      --column=COLUMN             Postgres column mapping of your configuration
                                  file on Postgres (may be repeated)
  -f, --format="yaml"             Format of your input file (YAML, JSON or TOML)
  -k, --kind="file"               Kind of the configuration file (file, http,
                                  redis, gitlab, k8s, ...)
  -p, --path=STRING               Path to your Semaphore configuration file
                                  (local or remote)
      --auth-token=STRING         Authentication token to access your
                                  configuration file
      --repository-slug=STRING    Repository slug to access your configuration
                                  file on GitHub
      --branch=STRING             Branch to access your configuration file on
                                  GitHub
      --base-url=STRING           Base URL of your configuration file on Gitlab
      --bucket=STRING             Bucket of your configuration file on S3
      --item=STRING               Item of your configuration file on S3
      --url=STRING                URL of your configuration file on HTTP
      --method="GET"              HTTP method to access your configuration file
                                  on HTTP
      --body=STRING               Http body to access your configuration file on
                                  HTTP
      --flag=STRING               Name of the flag to evaluate, if empty we will
                                  return the evaluation of all the flags
      --ctx="{}"                  Evaluation context in JSON format
      --object=STRING             Object of your configuration file on GCS
      --namespace="default"       Namespace of your configuration file on K8s
      --config-map=STRING         Config map of your configuration file on K8s
      --key=STRING                Key of your configuration file on K8s
      --uri=STRING                URI of your configuration file
      --database=STRING           Database of your configuration file on MongoDB
      --collection=STRING         Collection of your configuration file on
                                  MongoDB
      --container=STRING          Container of your configuration file on Azure
                                  Blob Storage
      --account-name=STRING       Account name of your configuration file on
                                  Azure Blob Storage
      --account-key=STRING        Account key of your configuration file on
                                  Azure Blob Storage
      --table=STRING              Postgres table of your configuration file on
                                  Postgres
      --timeout=0                 Timeout in seconds to access your
                                  configuration file on HTTP
      --check-mode                Check only mode - returns the configuration of
                                  spanned retriever without evaluating
